IMPORT prelude

-- Redemptorist Fathers Ordinance 1948 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Titular Superior of the Redemptorist Fathers in
-- Singapore" is, and who stands in for him while the office is vacant (s 2(1), (3)); what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do
-- (ss 2(2), 3); how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 4); what a Gazette notification proves (s 5); and whose rights the
-- Ordinance leaves alone (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RFO1948.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 6; the Legislative History names Act 7 of 1997 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act
-- 1997, s 6 read with item (29) of the First Schedule, in force 1 October 1997). The Ordinance is No. 9 of 1948, commenced 23 March
-- 1948. Section numbers follow the body (s 1 short title to s 6 saving); the arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is
-- shifted by one line by the PDF extraction.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0245 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Ordinance is six sections long, so all of it except the short title is in scope. For a person outside the Congregation it
-- matters when buying, leasing or lending on the security of the Corporation's property (s 3(1)), when suing it or being sued by it
-- about that property (s 3(2)), and in checking that a deed of the Corporation was executed by the right person, including while the
-- office of Titular Superior is vacant (ss 2(3), 4, 5).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 4(1) refers
-- (whether a power of attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); how a Titular Superior or a Reverend Father
-- Minister is appointed, about which the Ordinance says nothing; what "formal assumption of office" (s 2(3)) involves (taken as a stated
-- fact); the reference to "the Courts of the Colony of Singapore" (s 3(2)), read here simply as the courts; the Corporation's internal
-- governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Redemptorist Fathers Ordinance 1948 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 2(3) -- who is the Corporation, and who stands in during a vacancy`

-- s 2(1): "The Reverend Father William Dowling the Titular Superior of the Redemptorist Fathers in the Colony of Singapore, and his
-- successors in office, shall be a body corporate (hereinafter called 'the Corporation')", named "The Titular Superior of the
-- Redemptorist Fathers in Singapore", with perpetual succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 2(3): "The expression 'successors in office' shall be deemed to include the Reverend Father Minister from the time when the office
-- of 'The Titular Superior of the Redemptorist Fathers in Singapore' becomes vacant by the resignation or death of the holder for the
-- time being, until the formal assumption of office by his successor."
--
-- The deeming reaches only a vacancy "by the resignation or death" of the holder. A vacancy arising any other way (removal, recall or
-- transfer by the Congregation, for instance) is not mentioned; on the words, the Father Minister is not then deemed a successor in
-- office. That is a literal reading; whether a court would read the list as exhaustive is not known here.
-- A successor who has been appointed but has not yet formally assumed office is not yet the holder: the Father Minister remains the
-- deemed successor "until the formal assumption of office by his successor".
DECLARE Vacancy IS ONE OF
    `the office is filled`
    `vacant by resignation of the holder`
    `vacant by death of the holder`
    `vacant for another reason`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the Titular Superior in office`
    `the Reverend Father Minister`
    `a successor appointed but not yet formally in office`
    `a former Titular Superior`
    `another Redemptorist Father`

GIVEN `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacant` IF
    CONSIDER `the vacancy`
    WHEN `the office is filled` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vacancy is one section 2(3) covers` IF
    CONSIDER `the vacancy`
    WHEN `vacant by resignation of the holder` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `vacant by death of the holder` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `the state of the office` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Corporation's office-holder` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the Titular Superior in office` THEN NOT `the office is vacant` `the state of the office`
    WHEN `the Reverend Father Minister` THEN `the vacancy is one section 2(3) covers` `the state of the office`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2(2) and 3 -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed and altered, and made anew as to the Corporation seems fit."
-- s 3(1): "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, exchange, surrender, yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer, or otherwise dispose of any movable or
-- immovable property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit."
-- s 3(2): "The Corporation may sue and be sued in respect of such property in any of the Courts of the Colony of Singapore."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". The power to sue and be sued is "in respect of such
-- property"; the encoding takes "such property" to be the property of s 3(1) held by or vested in the Corporation (an inference) and
-- gives no power to sue or be sued about anything else. It returns FALSE for powers the Ordinance does not grant; whether the general
-- law supplies them to a body corporate is outside the text and not encoded.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `break, change or remake its corporate seal`
    `acquire, purchase or take property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `convey or assign property`
    `exchange property`
    `surrender or yield up property`
    `mortgage property`
    `demise property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue in respect of its property`
    `be sued in respect of its property`
    `sue or be sued on a matter not about its property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `break, change or remake its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire, purchase or take property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `convey or assign property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `exchange property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `surrender or yield up property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `demise property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `sue in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `be sued in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 4(1): "All deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the
-- Corporation in the presence of the Titular Superior for the time being of the Redemptorist Fathers in Singapore, or when the office
-- is vacant in the presence of the Reverend Father Minister, as the case may be, or the attorney of any one of them duly authorised by a
-- power of attorney deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, and shall also be signed by the said
-- Titular Superior ... or by the said Reverend Father Minister, as the case may be, or the attorney of any one of them so authorised".
-- s 4(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the said seal was duly and properly affixed, and that the
-- same is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- s 4(1) says "when the office is vacant" with no limit to resignation or death, so the Father Minister may seal and sign during ANY
-- vacancy, although s 2(3) deems him a successor in office only after a resignation or death. That mismatch is encoded as written.
-- "as the case may be" is read as: the Titular Superior (or his deposited attorney) while the office is filled, the Father Minister
-- (or his deposited attorney) while it is vacant. Reading "the attorney of any one of them" as limited by "as the case may be" is an
-- inference. An attorney whose power was never deposited does not qualify. Witness and signer need not be the same person on the words
-- of s 4(1); that reading is encoded.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Titular Superior for the time being`
    `the Reverend Father Minister acting`
    `a deposited attorney of the Titular Superior`
    `a deposited attorney of the Father Minister`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `another Redemptorist Father acting`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the office stands` IS A Vacancy
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer, `the office state` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may seal and sign for the Corporation` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Titular Superior for the time being` THEN NOT `the office is vacant` `the office state`
    WHEN `a deposited attorney of the Titular Superior` THEN NOT `the office is vacant` `the office state`
    WHEN `the Reverend Father Minister acting` THEN `the office is vacant` `the office state`
    WHEN `a deposited attorney of the Father Minister` THEN `the office is vacant` `the office state`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 4 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may seal and sign for the Corporation` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`) (`the instrument`'s `the office stands`)
    AND `may seal and sign for the Corporation` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) (`the instrument`'s `the office stands`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may seal and sign for the Corporation` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`) (`the instrument`'s `the office stands`)

§§ `5 -- what the Gazette proves`

-- s 5: "A notification in the Gazette of the appointment of any person to exercise the office of Titular Superior of the Redemptorist
-- Fathers in the Colony of Singapore, or of Reverend Father Minister, as the case may be, shall be conclusive evidence that such person
-- was duly authorised to exercise the said office in the Colony."
--
-- The notification proves authorisation only for the office it names. It speaks in the past tense ("was duly authorised") and says
-- nothing about whether the person is still in office (an inference from the wording, not stated).
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `the office of Titular Superior`
    `the office of Reverend Father Minister`

DECLARE Notification IS ONE OF
    `gazetted as Titular Superior`
    `gazetted as Reverend Father Minister`
    `not gazetted`

GIVEN `the office exercised` IS AN Office, `the notification` IS A Notification
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
    CONSIDER `the office exercised`
    WHEN `the office of Titular Superior` THEN
        CONSIDER `the notification`
        WHEN `gazetted as Titular Superior` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `the office of Reverend Father Minister` THEN
        CONSIDER `the notification`
        WHEN `gazetted as Reverend Father Minister` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government, all bodies politic and corporate, and all others, except
-- such as are mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
